{{also|tipoff|tip-off}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-tip off.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive}} To [[alert]] or [[inform]] someone, especially [[confidentially]].
#: ''An anonymous caller '''tipped off''' the police that the suspect would be in the area.''
# {{lb|en|basketball}} To put the ball in play by throwing it up between two opponents.
## {{lb|en|of a sports match}} To begin.
##: ''The game '''tips off''' in an hour, so hurry back!''
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[pour out]] (liquor); to tip the vessel and drink until it is empty.
#{{lb|en|transitive|and|intransitive|[[painting]]}} To use a particular brush technique for producing a flawless surface on a wet coat of paint.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to alert or inform someone}} {{l|en|inform}}, {{l|en|grass up}}, {{l|en|snitch}}; See also [[Thesaurus:rat out]]
* {{sense|to use a painting technique}} {{l|en|lay off}}

===See also===
* {{l|en|tip-off}} (noun)
* ''Synonym for [[lay off]]''

